Drop upstream's `[install] optimize = 1`.

It makes setuptools byte-compile the wheel's .opt-1.pyc files in a child
interpreter that runs `from distutils.util import byte_compile`; under the
forge cross env on Python 3.12+ (no stdlib distutils, setuptools' shim not
loaded in that child) this aborts the build after the extension compiled.
The .opt-1.pyc files are dead weight on mobile anyway.

--- a/setup.cfg	2026-09-30 23:49:10
+++ b/setup.cfg	2026-10-01 22:04:53
@@ -1,6 +1,3 @@
-[install]
-optimize = 1
-
 [metadata]
 description_file = README.md
 
